        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(xai): apply request policy to video generation requests",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users generating video with xAI could configure provider request policy, such as custom headers or proxy settings, but xAI video generation requests ignored that policy.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe xAI video provider now sanitizes `cfg.models.providers.xai.request` and passes it into the existing provider HTTP resolver used by the create, poll, and download flow. The change is limited to request policy wiring and leaves generation parameters, polling semantics, idempotency headers, and media parsing unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers who depend on configured provider transport policy can expect xAI video generation to honor those request settings. Default behavior is unchanged when no request policy is configured.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/xai/video-generation-provider.test.ts` passed: 19 tests.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local --engine claude --model claude-fable-5 --thinking high` reported no accepted/actionable findings.\n\n### 2026-07-12 follow-up: local controlled request-policy proof\n\n- Commit `523f5999e4` fixes the review gap by passing the resolved xAI request policy through video create, poll, and generated-video download. The poll/download stages now use guarded provider fetches when `allowPrivateNetwork` or a dispatcher/proxy policy is configured, while preserving the existing unconfigured fast path and bounded xAI JSON/media readers.\n- Local focused proof: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/xai/video-generation-provider.test.ts` passed: 19 tests.\n- The focused regression now asserts the configured header, explicit private-network opt-in, and dispatcher policy are visible on all three changed stages: create submit, status poll, and generated-video download.\n- This is controlled local provider-path proof only. No live xAI API call was made and no real xAI account, proxy, or media generation was exercised.\n\n## Proof\n\n### 2026-07-12 current-head local proof after update-branch\n\n- Exact head tested: `08bdeda0cd039a1e01de1e49e02bbebd8ac1337d`\n- Scope: Controlled local proof for xAI video generation request-policy forwarding. The current head fixes the real request-policy bug found by the transport proof: `request.allowPrivateNetwork=true` is no longer overridden by a caller-level `allowPrivateNetwork:false`. The proof uses a local HTTP server as the xAI API origin and generated-video URL; it is not a live xAI request.\n- Commands:\n\n  ```bash\n  git fetch fork alix/xai-request-policy-video-generation && git checkout --detach FETCH_HEAD\n  git diff --check\n  node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs --tsconfig config/tsconfig/oxlint.extensions.json extensions/xai/video-generation-provider.ts extensions/xai/video-generation-provider.test.ts extensions/xai/video-generation-provider.transport.test.ts\n  node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/xai/video-generation-provider.transport.test.ts extensions/xai/video-generation-provider.test.ts\n  ```\n\n- Result: PASS: `git diff --check` passed; focused oxlint passed; Vitest passed 1 shard, 2 test files, 20 tests in 29.45s total wall time including local heavy-check lock wait; Vitest duration 12.67s.\n- Observation: `extensions/xai/video-generation-provider.transport.test.ts` starts a local HTTP server and drives the real provider path through video create, poll, and generated-video download. The configured xAI custom header reaches the create and poll API-origin requests, while the generated-video download request does not include the custom header or Authorization header. The existing unit test also asserts the download init is headerless and that `resolveProviderHttpRequestConfig` is no longer called with a hard `allowPrivateNetwork:false` override.\n- Not tested: No live xAI video generation job, real API key, proxy, media generation account, or external provider endpoint was exercised.\n",
        "branch": "alix/xai-request-policy-video-generation",
